---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "") + "/";
const cases = [
  { id: "1", title: "Case 1", file: "delman-sequential-case1.png" },
  { id: "2", title: "Case 2", file: "delman-sequential-case2.png" },
];
---

<div class="sequence-panel">
  <div class="panel-header">
    <h3>Four successive safety edits</h3>
    <span class="source-label">Figure 8</span>
  </div>
  <div class="sequence-grid">
    {
      cases.map((c) => (
        <figure class="sequence-case" aria-label={c.title}>
          <img
            src={base + "figures/" + c.file}
            alt={`${c.title}: HarmBench attack success over four successive DELMAN edits, showing the full dataset and individual edited behavior categories.`}
            width="4000"
            height="2500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">
    Sequential editing on Llama2-7B-chat under GCG. Each case applies four
    successive edits, with ASR tracked across the full HarmBench dataset and all
    six behavior categories.
  </p>
</div>
<details class="evidence-details">
  <summary
    ><span>Sequential edits: safety and utility</span><span>Table 10</span
    ></summary
  ><div class="details-body">
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="result-table">
        <thead
          ><tr
            ><th scope="col">Editing strategy</th><th scope="col">MT-Bench ↑</th
            >{
              [
                "HarmBench",
                "AdvBench",
                "JailbreakBench",
                "MaliciousInstruct",
              ].map((name) => (
                <th scope="col">
                  {name}
                  <br />
                  ASR (%) ↓
                </th>
              ))
            }</tr
          ></thead
        ><tbody>
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">DELMAN</th><td>6.31</td><td>0%</td><td>0%</td><td
              >0%</td
            ><td>1%</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Sequential · Case 1</th><td>6.35</td><td>3%</td><td
              >0%</td
            ><td>10%</td><td>0%</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><th scope="row">Sequential · Case 2</th><td>6.64</td><td>4%</td><td
              >5%</td
            ><td>6%</td><td>0%</td></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div><p class="table-note">
      Llama2-7B-chat under GCG. DELMAN uses the full editing set, while sequential
      variants apply four category specific edits.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>
